  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. The code typechecks. I could not run `vite build` or view a render, so the look and the shader compile are untested.\n\n- **Shield:** a 3-unit sphere with a `material.custom` GLSL shader. It has a cyan fresnel rim, scanlines in world-height that scroll upward using `uTime`, and a slower bright band that sweeps up. It is translucent: alpha-blended, double-sided, no depth write.\n- **Cube:** a metallic rounded cube inside the sphere, rotated every frame through `app.nodes.require(\"cube\").setRotation`.\n- **Scene:** a dark background and a glossy dark floor. A cyan point light under the cube casts glow onto the floor, and there is a neutral environment, a key light and bloom. The camera frames the sphere.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and one animation frame. I avoided top-level `await` because there is no vite config and the default build target may reject it.\n\nThe floor glow comes from the point light on a glossy floor, not a real reflection.\n\n",
